[%emt 0:00:28] [%think 1840] [%out 2060] [%in 2] [%cacheread 0]
[%cachewrite 2129] Keep the rook behind the black pawn on a3 and on the 7th
rank, where it cuts off the black king. Move the white king to b4 to watch the
a-pawn. - **If black plays ...Rb1+**: the a3 pawn loses its protection, and
Kxa3 wins it. - **If black plays ...a2**: Kb3 returns. The a2 pawn is then
attacked by both the king and the rook, and black cannot promote it. Other
moves are worse. Rxa3 allows Rxa3+ Kxa3, and black's f-pawn then wins. Kb2 is
illegal because the a3 pawn covers b2. } 46... a2 47. Kb3 { [%emt 0:00:17]
